# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: VargaMarionPath | Scene: VargaPath9

translate es strings:

    old "Spymaster Kravel had been left behind at Reinmeer to manage the city in her absence. She hoped he would prove worthy of her trust in him."
    new "El espía jefe Kravel había sido dejado atrás en Reinmeer para gestionar la ciudad en su ausencia. Esperaba que demostrara ser digno de su confianza."

    old "Varga, as head of the army and her husband, could not have remained behind. Regardless, Sarah was glad he was there to support her."
    new "Varga, como jefe del ejército y su esposo, no podía quedarse atrás. De todos modos, Sarah estaba contenta de que estuviera allí para apoyarla."

    old "Sarah had said a prayer, both for her husband and her brother, praying that somehow both would be kept safe amidst the carnage that would follow."
    new "Sarah había dicho una oración, tanto para su esposo como para su hermano, suplicando que de algún modo ambos fueran mantenidos a salvo entre la carnicería que seguiría."

    old "On the route to Dianthus, her army experienced no serious obstacles."
    new "En el camino a Dianthus, su ejército no encontró ningún obstáculo serio."

    old "Even crossing over the river and past the province border, they faced no attack."
    new "Incluso cruzando el río y pasando la frontera de la provincia, no enfrentaron ningún ataque."

    old "Sarah was standing alone on a small hill, overlooking the battlefield, while all around her, the army prepared."
    new "Sarah estaba sola en una pequeña colina, mirando el campo de batalla, mientras que a su alrededor, el ejército se preparaba."

    old "Hello there, husband."
    new "Hola, esposo."

    old "Ooh, am I in trouble, my lady?"
    new "Oh, ¿estoy en problemas, mi señora?"

    old "Sarah. You know that I would do anything for you, that I would do anything to keep you safe."
    new "Sarah. Sabes que haría cualquier cosa por ti, que haría cualquier cosa para mantenerte a salvo."

    old "So trust me, I wouldn't be leading your army today if I thought we would lose."
    new "Confía en mí; no estaría al mando de tu ejército hoy si pensara que perderíamos."

    old "They like to pretend that it has never been conquered since it was first built, but that's not true."
    new "Les gusta fingir que nunca ha sido conquistada desde su construcción inicial, pero eso no es cierto."

    old "I read that it's been conquered many times since, it's just that every family that drives out the other one, pretends that they've lived there forever."
    new "Leí que ha sido conquistada muchas veces desde entonces, solo que cada familia que expulsa a la otra afirma haber vivido allí para siempre."

    old "Before the Achillea's took it, some other family did."
    new "Antes de que la familia Achillea lo tomara, otra familia lo hizo."

    old "Maybe, a bit here and there. I think you've ruined me. I can never go back to living on a farm ever again."
    new "Quizá, un poco por aquí y por allá. Creo que me has estropeado. Nunca podré volver a vivir en una granja otra vez."

    old "Sarah reached out with her hand, touching Varga's strong arm for comfort."
    new "Sarah tendió la mano y tocó el fuerte brazo de Varga para darle consuelo."

    old "But please, tell me that you will stay safe. I can't lose you."
    new "Pero por favor, dímelo que te mantendrás a salvo. No puedo perderte."

    old "Varga placed one arm around her."
    new "Varga le colocó un brazo alrededor de ella."

    old "I'll come back to you, trust me on that."
    new "Volveré por ti, créeme."

    old "A head on assault on the fort would be a disaster."
    new "Un asalto frontal al fuerte sería una catástrofe."

    old "Sarah listened intently as her husband went over the strategy."
    new "Sarah escuchó atentamente mientras su esposo repasaba la estrategia."

    old "She turned to Varga and kissed him."
    new "Se volvió hacia Varga y lo besó."

    old "She watched as her husband turned to leave, going back down the hill."
    new "Sarah observó cómo su esposo se giraba para irse, bajando la colina."

    old "But by fortune or divine intervention, it would not take that long."
    new "Pero por fortuna o intervención divina, no sería necesario tanto tiempo."

    old "Striking the supply room filled to the brim with siege oil."
    new "Golpeando el almacén de suministros, lleno hasta el borde con aceite de asedio."

    old "All witnessed as suddenly, it was as though a new sun arose."
    new "Todos presenciaron cómo, de repente, parecía surgir un nuevo sol."

    old "Darkness dissapeared as a rush of light rushed out from inside the wall, bright and full of fury."
    new "La oscuridad desapareció cuando un torrente de luz brotó desde dentro del muro, brillante y llena de furia."

    old "Great slabs of stone did not simply come loose, but were flung across the sky as though they weighed nothing."
    new "Grandes losas de piedra no se desprendieron simplemente, sino que fueron lanzadas a través del cielo como si pesaran nada."

    old "Don't worry, lady Sarah. Your husband is as skilled a swordsmen as any."
    new "No te preocupes, bella Sarah. Tu marido es tan diestro con la espada como cualquier otro."

    old "Near the entrance, she saw Varga and rushed up towards him. Thank the gods."
    new "Cerca de la entrada, vio a Varga y se lanzó hacia él. Gracias a los dioses."

    old "As she ran up to her husband and seized his arm, she realized he did not react, instead, only looking towards the other end of the room."
    new "Como ella se acercó a su esposo y agarró su brazo, notó que no reaccionaba; en cambio, solo miraba el otro extremo de la habitación."

    old "The words were like a whisper."
    new "Las palabras fueron como un susurro."

    old "And then you decide to marry this creature."
    new "Y luego decides casarte con esta criatura."

    old "Marion gestured with his blade towards Varga."
    new "Marion señaló con su espada hacia ella."

    old "For what? Love?"
    new "¿Por qué? ¿Amor?"

    old "All your ancestors knew they had greater obligation, one to their nation, but you only think about yourself."
    new "Todos tus antepasados sabían que tenían una obligación mayor, hacia su nación, pero tú solo piensas en ti mismo."

    old "Reason with him."
    new "Razón con él."

    old "You kill my brother, and you and your family will live in infamy for centuries."
    new "Matas a mi hermano, y tú y tu familia viviréis en infamia durante siglos."

    old "Offer him mercy"
    new "Ofrecerle misericordia"

    old "Yes...I accept...I will go into exile."
    new "Sí... acepto... iré al exilio."

    old "Her husband has his arm around her shoulder."
    new "Su esposo tiene el brazo alrededor de su hombro."

    old "The soldiers will bring him with us, back home, to Castle Reinmeer, where he belongs. He'll be safe there, alright?"
    new "Los soldados lo traerán con nosotros, a casa, al Castillo Reinmeer, donde pertenece. Allí estará seguro, ¿verdad?"
